egories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"ZOZ94_vjuogm6PzmuIa1FQ","review_id":"6pBU6YPPzhUwlBaDoPNQHg","date":"2021-01-03T22:45:01","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9366658926010132,"text_excerpt":"Stumbled across this place after my first choice for pho turned out to be closed. It was nice to try something new. It has a stylish dining area. Large, good for groups, and complete with TVs. There's both Vietnamese and sushi available, so it seems to be fusion of sorts. I ordered the tofu broccoli rice plate and it was a heaping portion. The sauce was delicious and there is hoisin at every table which of course I made use of. My friend tried the sashimi and some kind of mixed fish sushi roll, and seemed pleased with both. I would definitely come back and probably will as it isn't too far from home."},{"business_id":"ZOZ94_vjuogm6PzmuIa1FQ","review_id":"lMgy59pGlvK4ai8mnbNEyw","date":"2013-12-01T03:40:21","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9249956011772156,"text_excerpt":"Went here for lunch, great to find a good Vietnamese place In the CBD. Enjoyed the vermecelli salad, looking forward to trying the pho next time."},{"business_id":"ZOZ94_vjuogm6PzmuIa1FQ","review_id":"_A2eSQbhCAu8bUHs6xl20g","date":"2013-10-23T15:33:06","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9249718189239502,"text_excerpt":"If you find yourself in the CBD and get a craving for Vietnamese food, your options are somewhat limited. Viet Orleans may be one of your only downtown options, but that doesn't mean it isn't good. I have been very happy with everything I have sampled thus far. The Food Banh Mi - Their version of the popular Vietnamese Po-Boy is slightly different than what I was used to, but in a good way. Most places use a small baguette style loaf for the sandwiches whereas Viet Orleans uses actual Leidenheimer French Bread. Instead of having to order two small 